cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HomoeoGWAS, please cite the software release you used. A bioRxiv preprint is in preparation."
title: "HomoeoGWAS: subgenome-aware trait architecture and homoeolog-interaction analysis for allopolyploid crops"
abstract: >-
  HomoeoGWAS analyses allopolyploid crop panels by modelling each subgenome
  explicitly. A subgenome-stratified multi-kernel mixed model partitions trait
  variance among subgenomes and runs a leave-one-chromosome-out per-SNP scan.
  A gene-resolution homoeolog interaction test scores every pair of homoeologous
  copies with omniB (minor burden, PC1 and kernel-Hadamard encodings) and
  calibrates all edges or groups as one experiment-wide bootstrap-minP family
  with a kinship-preserving, heteroscedasticity-robust null. An evidence audit
  labels each result, and a CLI, an MCP server and an AI-agent skill drive the
  workflows.
type: software
